messages:
sam: Quick follow-up to the RFC — we still need concrete SDK surface decisions for pagination + retries across Python/TS/Go. What should the primitives be?

miriam: Good call. We left open server cursor vs offset + how retries should interplay with iterators.

raj: My take: expose a tiny transport abstraction (sync/async depending on language) and build the paging helpers on top. Transport should be responsible for low-level retries; iterators handle resume semantics.

alex: Concern: if transport retries transparently, how do we avoid duplicate items when paging? Example: client fetches page N, server processes but response times out — retry might return same items. We need a resume token from the server or monotonic item ids.

sam: Agreed. Prefer server-provided opaque cursor that points to the next position. SDK should persist the last successful `next_cursor`. That lets us retry the page request safely.

miriam: Proposal: require paged endpoints to return { items: [...], next_cursor: string | null }. For streaming endpoints we can keep stream semantics but document that resume is only supported for paged endpoints.

raj: Implementation notes: transport API (pseudo):
```
// TS/py: send(req) -> Response | AsyncIterable<ResponseChunk>
transport.send(req, {stream: false}) => Response
transport.send(req, {stream: true}) => AsyncIterable<Chunk>
```
SDK pager will call transport.send for each page request and apply retry policy on non-streaming page fetches.

alex: Retry policy specifics: default max_attempts=5, exponential backoff with full jitter, retry on 429/503/504/502. Important: do NOT retry on 4xx other than 429. Also honor `Retry-After` when present.

sam: For paged endpoints, SDK should: (1) call page request, (2) if error retry the whole request, (3) when success, yield items and save `next_cursor`. If user stops iteration we should surface the last known cursor via an attribute on the iterator so callers can persist it.

raj: Language surfaces: short sketches — keep them tiny.
Python:
```
def list_items(client, start_cursor=None):
    cursor = start_cursor
    while True:
        resp = client._transport.request_pages(cursor=cursor)
        for it in resp.items:
            yield it
        if not resp.next_cursor:
            break
        cursor = resp.next_cursor
    # iterator object could expose .resume_cursor = cursor
```
TypeScript (async iterator):
```
async function* listItems(client, startCursor?: string) {
  let cursor = startCursor;
  while (true) {
    const resp = await client._transport.fetchPage({cursor});
    for (const i of resp.items) yield i;
    if (!resp.next_cursor) break;
    cursor = resp.next_cursor;
  }
}
// exposing resume: attach property to the returned async iterator object
```
Go:
```
func ListItems(ctx context.Context, client *Client, startCursor string) <-chan Item {
  out := make(chan Item)
  go func(){
    defer close(out)
    cursor := startCursor
    for {
      resp, _ := client.transport.FetchPage(ctx, cursor)
      for _, it := range resp.Items { out <- it }
      if resp.NextCursor == "" { return }
      cursor = resp.NextCursor
    }
  }()
  return out
}
```

miriam: Important: generator/iterator should expose a tiny metadata API: `.resume_cursor` or `.last_cursor` so callers can checkpoint. Document pattern for resuming after crashes.

alex: Streaming endpoints: if server supports chunked streaming with per-item ids, we can attempt dedupe when reconnecting by passing `since_id` but don't promise perfect exactly-once. Document eventual duplication possibility for streams.

sam: Backpressure: in TS/py async iterators the user will control pull rate. For Go channels we should provide a buffered channel default (size 16) and let callers handle blocking.

raj: Edge-case: partial page returned because server cut connection mid-page. Our approach: server MUST include `next_cursor` when it can; otherwise treat page as retriable (client retries whole page). We should ask API team to always emit next_cursor even for partial pages (cursor-v2).

infra-bot: deploy-bot: canary updated pagination service to return cursor-v2 on /v2/list and added item_id in chunks.

miriam: Action items: (1) update API spec to mandate `next_cursor` on paged endpoints (2) add resume_cursor to SDK iterators in Python/TS/Go (3) default retry policy doc + config (4) tests for dedupe/resume.

alex: +1 on action items. I'll draft the API spec change and add examples.

sam: Sounds good. If we agree I'll take SDK PR to implement iterator attribute and default retry config. :thumbsup:
